From 2a6968b40378dca5650e18e03ad0407738c47be5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advertising: Fix sending extra bytes with MGMT_OP_ADD_EXT_ADV_DATA

The extended advertising data command was sized with struct
mgmt_cp_add_advertising, which is 8 bytes larger than struct
mgmt_cp_add_ext_adv_data, so bluetoothd sent 8 trailing bytes after the
scan response. Kernels since d3f7d17960ed ("Bluetooth: MGMT: validate
Add Extended Advertising Data length") reject the command with Invalid
Parameters, and every LEAdvertisingManager1.RegisterAdvertisement fails
with org.bluez.Error.Failed. The pinned 6.12.93 Raspberry Pi kernel has
that check and the Improv Wi-Fi provisioner restarted every five seconds.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/bluez/bluez/commit/2a6968b40378dca5650e18e03ad0407738c47be5]
---
 src/advertising.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/advertising.c
+++ b/src/advertising.c
@@ -1364,8 +1364,7 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	param_len = sizeof(struct mgmt_cp_add_advertising) + adv_data_len +
-							scan_rsp_len;
+	param_len = sizeof(*cp) + adv_data_len + scan_rsp_len;
 
 	cp = malloc0(param_len);
 	if (!cp) {
